linux-redmi-marble (7.2.8+marble13) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Enable USB-C dual-role on marble (usb-c-connector-dual-role.patch).
    pmic-glink had no connector@0, so dwc3's usb-role-switch had no consumer
    and the port stayed dr_mode=peripheral: a U-disk plugged into the phone
    was never enumerated. Add the connector, wire port@0 to usb_1_dwc3_hs,
    and set dr_mode=otg with role-switch-default-mode=peripheral so netboot
    keeps its device default. Verified on hardware: usb_role switches to
    host and xhci-hcd enumerates a USB-C audio device.

