linux-redmi-marble (7.2.8+marble12) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Expose the HEVC/H.264 deblocking filter controls the HFI gen2 encoder
    needs (iris-deblocking-filter-controls.patch, from FFT-infra/
    qualcomm-iris-vaapi packaging/kernel/0002). Without them a VA-API client
    cannot set the loop filter mode or its alpha/beta (H.264) and tc/beta
    (HEVC) offsets: iris only registered the entropy and bitrate caps for
    encoder sessions, so vaCreateConfig() for VAEntrypointEncSlice either
    failed or silently used firmware defaults. The controls are registered in
    inst_fw_cap_sm8550_enc, reject changes once OUTPUT is streaming, and are
    packed into HFI_PROP_DEBLOCKING_MODE biased by six.
  * Keep the timestamps of error buffers (iris-preserve-timestamps-on-error-
    buffers.patch, same source, 0004). An encoder that returns a
    CORRUPT/ERROR buffer with a zeroed timestamp breaks the client's
    frame-to-packet mapping on the first dropped frame.
  * Note for whoever refreshes debian/patches: iris-decode-order-output and
    ath11k-load-wlan-mac-from-firmware no longer patch the 7.2.8 tree - iLtanaka
    merged both upstream. debian/rules already reverse-tests each patch and
    prints "already applied", so they stay for older base commits at no cost.

 -- GhfunNiHe <131235947+GhfunNiHe@users.noreply.github.com>  Sat, 24 Oct 2026 14:05:00 +0800

linux-redmi-marble (7.2.8+marble11) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Enable CONFIG_DMABUF_HEAPS + CONFIG_DMABUF_HEAPS_SYSTEM (/dev/dma_heap/
    system). The new Iris VA-API backend uses the system heap for the
    driver-owned scratch buffer an Import CAPTURE pool lends the firmware
    during a STOP/LAST drain, and as the last-resort fallback in
    allocate_stable(). Import is the publish policy this device takes for
    H.264/HEVC whenever the decode-order controls are present, so without the
    heap the zero-copy path fails with "allocate scratch CAPTURE buffer" on
    the first seek or EOS - playback ends in a decode error instead of a
    clean EOS. The MSM GEM path allocate_stable() tries first is unaffected;
    this only fills in what had no other source.
  * Ship together with libva-v4l2 1.0.0-3: the previous backend never touched
    /dev/dma_heap, so the pairing matters, not the individual packages.

