linux-redmi-marble (7.2.8+marble4) unstable; urgency=medium

  * postinst no longer hardcodes root=PARTLABEL=linux in the extlinux.conf it
    writes to the ESP. It now takes the root source from the "/" entry of
    /etc/fstab, which is where the rootfs build (and the user) picks the
    partition; PARTLABEL=/UUID=/LABEL=/dev/... all pass through verbatim.
    Falls back to the root= already on the ESP, then to PARTLABEL=linux.
    This removes the coupling that forced the same partition name to be
    written by hand in two repositories, and keeps extlinux.conf in sync with
    fstab on an on-device apt upgrade.

